        "procedure": "0.75 mmol La(NO3)3·6H2O (0.324 g), 0.75 mmol 8-hydroxyquinoline (0.108 g), and 1 mmol sodium azide (0.064 g) were dissolved in 15 mL C2H5OH:H2O (1:1). The solution was sealed in a 25 mL Teflon-lined stainless steel autoclave and heated at 140 °C for 3 days. After cooling to room temperature, yellow crystals of 1 were isolated by filtration, washed with ethanol several times, and dried in air.",
